1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,090
Hi guys.

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,300
Today let's have a closer look at present continuous.

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:09,200
I am doing I am speaking.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,810
I am teaching right now.

5
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:18,710
So we use present continuous to talk about something that we do at the moment.

6
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:26,510
We often use it with words like now currently at the moment as we speak.

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,070
Okay.

8
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:34,760
Also we can use present continuous to talk about events in the future.

9
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:40,400
For example, I am meeting Tom at four.

10
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:44,210
So this will happen in the future.

11
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,090
But it's a plan.

12
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:50,510
It's an arrangement that Tom and I made.

13
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,710
So we know this is happening.

14
00:00:52,730 --> 00:01:04,010
I am meeting Tom at four or for example, we are having an online interview in 30 minutes.

15
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,040
This will happen in the future.

16
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,560
This will happen in 30 minutes.

17
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,700
But we can use present continuous to talk about it.

18
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:17,990
Or I am having a lunch with Kelly.

19
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:24,470
I'm having a lunch with Kelly in the future, but I use present continuous to talk about it.

20
00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:25,580
Good.

21
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:29,070
Now let's play a short game.

22
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:29,780
Okay.

23
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:31,970
The rules of this game.

24
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:36,890
I say a sentence in present simple.

25
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:44,010
Your job is to say the same sentence, but in present continuous.

26
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:48,240
And you can add phrases like now at the moment.

27
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:50,310
Let's see an example.

28
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,770
I speak to students every day.

29
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:01,210
I am speaking to students right now.

30
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:02,660
Okay.

31
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:03,410
Ready?

32
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:06,740
Three, two, one.

33
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:12,040
I work on tasks every day.

34
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:19,790
I am working on tasks now.

35
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:25,130
He checks pull requests often.

36
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,770
He is checking pull requests now.

37
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:36,540
She writes emails every Friday.

38
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:39,810
Yes.

39
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:43,530
She's writing emails right now.

40
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:49,090
We have demos on Mondays.

41
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,790
We are having a demo right now.

42
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,670
He is smart.

43
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:03,480
He is smart.

44
00:03:03,510 --> 00:03:10,350
This sentence doesn't change because now we talk about a state, not an action.

45
00:03:10,350 --> 00:03:15,780
So this sentence cannot be transformed in present continuous tense.

46
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,680
For example, I am a.

47
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:20,140
The same.

48
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:24,020
I'm a all the time or I am tall.

49
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:28,160
We cannot say the sentence using present continuous.

50
00:03:28,190 --> 00:03:29,430
Very good.

51
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:30,830
If you made a mistake.

52
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:32,330
Try again.

53
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:33,230
Thank you.

54
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:34,460
And see you next time.

55
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:35,480
Bye.
